From 865503382cf08e9599b45e93ffc2d0a6b6ca2ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:57:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Paste recently copied text from a clipboard history

The text copied while the app is in the foreground, and the text on the
clipboard when the app gets the focus, are kept in a history of the
last 20 copies, only in memory since they can be passwords. Swiping up
on the paste extra key, the tab bar settings menu or Ctrl+Shift+H show
it: tapping an item pastes it into the current tab, and a long press
copies it to the clipboard or deletes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
---
